Adapted and modified from TradingAgents 0.5.1:

  deerflow_bridge/data_tools.py
    Portions adapted from tradingagents/dataflows/vendors/fred.py: the curated
    FRED alias table with a descriptive phrase rejected before any API call,
    and both realtime bounds of every FRED request pinned to the earlier of
    the as-of date and the vendor's own date in America/Chicago. DRF modified
    the alias set, the id validation, the date handling (dates compared as
    date objects), the error classification, caching, rendering and
    secrecy rules.
    Portions adapted from tradingagents/dataflows/vendors/sec_edgar.py: the
    as-filed reading of SEC EDGAR XBRL company facts (only facts filed on or
    before the as-of date; tags tried in priority order, the first to report
    a period owns it and values are never summed across tags; quarter and
    fiscal-year span gates; a fiscal-year period must be reported by an
    annual-report form while the latest filing of any form supplies its
    value, so amendments and recasts count from their own filing date; no
    fourth quarter derived) and its statement tag lists. DRF modified the date
    handling (dates parsed and compared as date objects), the per-period
    units, the accession tie-break, the fail-closed post-condition, the line
    set, the identity rules, the error classification, caching, rendering
    and provenance.

  backend/tests/test_data_tools_edgar.py
    Fixtures modelled on tests/test_sec_edgar.py: the Apple restatement,
    filing-date, quarter/year-to-date, tag-fallback, twelve-month-total,
    quarter-end-balance, recast and capital-expenditure cases.

